KZ3 patch 2082: recompiled PPU stores into the RSX local window mark the texture page bitmap.

Pass 75's LD_TEX_WATCH run (work/proton/r75-chk) named the writer of the location-0 texture misses: vm_write64 on a
PPU thread storing into the 0x0FFxxxxx mip spans, which noted nothing (SPU puts, fs reads, NV0039/NV3089/NV308A and
write-backs do). Every PPU store now tests one byte per 64 KiB guest page (g_ppu_vm_page, the table of patch 1091)
for a new NOTE bit (0x10) after the store: vm_write8..64 through VM_WRITE_COH, and the lifted inline stores (stvx,
dcbz, stwbrx, sthbrx, stvebx/ehx/ewx) through PPU_ST_NOTE in the lifter preamble. A set bit calls ppu_store_note ->
the hook cellGcmSys installs at cellGcmInit (gcm_ppu_note_pages_ea -> rsx_live_draw_note_guest_write_pages(0, ...)),
which also sets the bit on the 256 MB local window. LD_PPU_STORE_NOTE=0 leaves the bits clear (old behaviour).
LD_TEX_WRITER tags the notes "ppu-store". Not covered: stwcx/stdcx reservation stores and host HLE writes.

Also LD_FEAT_LOG=1 counts volume textures (SET_TEXTURE_FORMAT dimension 3) per sampled unit: header volume=N
frames=F, rows "volume" with aux = depth<<24 | height<<12 | width (for upstream PR 335).

Host test: tools/smoke/test_ppu_store_note.sh (compiles the patch's own blocks; checks + ns/store timing).
Refreshed for v0.15.0 (SPU pass 85): upstream's lifter writes the byte-reversed and vector stores through
VM_RAW_ST / vm_raw_st16 (aligned single-copy atomic) instead of memcpy; the notes follow those, and the two direct
vm_base stores v0.15.0 added (stdbrx, stvlx/stvrx) note too.

